package CanvasNet {
    part def MarkBuilder {
        doc /* The internal MarkBuilder (a sealed partial class) with IsSupported (true for bar, rect, point, circle, square, rule, tick, line, area, trail, text, and arc) and Build, which reads the mark type (a string or the type of a mark definition), loops over the rows of the DataTable (cancellation polled every 1,024 rows, the scene budget charged for the marks group and each item before it is created), maps the channels x, y, color, fill, stroke, size, opacity, shape, strokeWidth, strokeDash, fillOpacity, strokeOpacity, and angle through the scale models (field, value, and datum forms), resolves the mark properties through the ResolvedConfig precedence chain, and creates the SceneRect, SceneSymbol, and SceneRule items of a marks group in the coordinates of the data rectangle: bars, rectangles, and ticks fill the band on a discrete position (at least minBandSize; step minus 2 on a point scale) and are centered with continuousBandSize or thickness on a continuous one, the measure axis runs from the value to zero (or, for a stacked channel and for an x2 or y2 range, from the start to the end), symbols sit at the band center or the value with the size as the area of the bounding box (at the upper end of a stack), and rules are full-width or full-height lines, stems to zero, or segments of a range; Phase 6 draws the stacked layers of the EncodingPlan from the start to the end value of each row, the x2 and y2 secondary channels of bar, rect, and rule marks (a field, a datum, or a pixel value; a row with an invalid end is not drawn), a bar or rect on a binned channel as the span of its bin less binSpacing (bar 1, rect and tick 0) with a half-pixel edge and a minimum of minBandSize, the bin midpoint for point-like marks, and the clip of the data rectangle when the x or y scale has an explicit array domain (unless clip is false); paint follows Vega-Lite (the mark color is the fill of a filled mark and the stroke of an unfilled one, colors from the ordinal, sequential, diverging, quantize, quantile, or threshold scale of the channel, default opacity 0.7 for point, circle, square, and tick). Phase 7 gives each row its stroke width, fill opacity, stroke opacity, and dash pattern (at most 64 entries; a longer one is a located VegaLiteRenderException) from the strokeWidth, fillOpacity, strokeOpacity, and strokeDash channels, and each point its shape (a symbol name; a custom path is kept and drawn as a circle) and each point, circle, or square its angle; a channel that the mark does not draw (shape, angle, strokeDash) is ignored. A row with a null, NaN, or non-numeric value on a channel with a continuous domain is not drawn. Exceeding MaxSceneItems is a VegaLiteRenderException with the location of the mark, and cancellation is polled every 1,024 rows. Phase 5 gives the constructor an optional RowExpressions (the compiled expressions and the evaluator of the call): the expr references of the drawn view's mark color, fill, stroke, opacity, strokeWidth, and size (point, circle, and square) and of the constant value of the color, fill, stroke, opacity, and size (point, circle, and square) channels are evaluated once per row against the transformed row, a text result being a color and a finite number an opacity, width, or size, any other result leaving the default; the tests of conditions are evaluated as described below and every other expression site is ignored (and reported by the FeatureCatalog). A row whose value a log, pow, sqrt, or symlog scale cannot map (zero on a log scale) has no position and is not drawn, and the bars of a log axis start at the start of the domain. A binned field draws each mark with the value of its scale at the start of the bin (the color of the bin of a bin-ordinal scale), and the bars of a histogram whose color bins the field as x does take the color of their bin. The test of every condition of a color, fill, stroke, opacity, fill opacity, stroke opacity, stroke width, stroke dash, size, shape, or angle channel is evaluated for every row by the expression engine under the step budget, the first condition that holds gives the value (or the scaled field), and a row for which none holds gets the value or scale of the channel or the default of the mark. Phase 8 draws the bar or rect of a field with a time unit on a time scale over its whole unit (from the start field to the end field of the plan, edges at lerp(start, end, (1 - band) / 2) and (1 + band) / 2 with band the relative width or timeUnitBandSize, the bar spacing, the minimum band size compared with the whole unit, and the half-pixel axis translate as for a bin), places the points, circles, squares, ticks, and rules of a time unit at lerp(start, end, bandPosition) (the start when no band position is defined, the middle for the ticks and bars by the default configuration), draws a rect-based mark whose band position is not one half at one half (the FeatureCatalog reports vl-encoding-bandposition-rect), and places the marks of a time scale at their dates. Phase 9 (MarkBuilder.Order.cs, MarkBuilder.Paths.cs, MarkBuilder.Overlays.cs, MarkBuilder.Text.cs, and MarkBuilder.Arcs.cs, partial files of the MarkBuilder and of its Run) makes IsSupported true for line, area, trail, text, and arc as well. A line, an area, or a trail is built from groups: the rows are read once (validity of the continuous channels, pixel positions kept even for an invalid row), counted into groups of equal values of EncodingPlan.PathGroupFields in the order of the first row, and each group is sorted stably by the order fields or the pixel position of the dimension, painted from its first defined row, charged to the scene budget (one item and the CurveBuilder.MaxSegments bound) before its segment list exists, and emitted as one ScenePath with segments (line: stroke, size as the stroke width; area: closed outline between the value and the baseline, the start of the stack, or the second channel, vertical or horizontal by the orient) or one SceneTrail with runs of points that carry the per-point size; the interpolate and tension properties choose the curve (an area with bundle falls back to linear), the invalid mode (default break-paths-show-path-domains) breaks the path at an invalid row or, for filter, connects the neighbors, and a group with fewer than two defined points draws nothing and costs nothing. The overlays are built by a second run with the overlay definition (point symbols on line, area, trail, and rule; a line on the top edge of an area; the 0.7 default opacity of an area with an overlay). The text mark creates one SceneText per row with the formatted label (d3 number and time formats through TimeLabels, bin ranges, JavaScript text, array and lineBreak lines, a limit of MaxStringLength per label and sixteen times that per mark), the Vega defaults, the font, angle, and offsets, and the polar offset of theta and radius. The arc mark creates one SceneArc per row from the theta and radius scales (stacked slices from the start to the end of the stack, a band scale across its band, the mark properties theta, theta2, radius, radius2, innerRadius, outerRadius, padAngle, and cornerRadius) around the center of the data rectangle or the x and y position. The order channel sorts the draw order of every other mark when the encoding is not stacked, and the dash, dash offset, cap, join, and miter limit reach every item type. */

        comment sourceRef /* Source: src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite/Marks/MarkBuilder.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite/Marks/MarkBuilder.Order.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite/Marks/MarkBuilder.Paths.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite/Marks/MarkBuilder.Overlays.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite/Marks/MarkBuilder.Text.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite/Marks/MarkBuilder.Arcs.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite/Marks/NamespaceDoc.cs */
        comment testRef /* Test: test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite.Tests/Marks/MarkBuilderTests.cs, test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite.Tests/Marks/MarkBuilderChannelTests.cs, test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite.Tests/Marks/MarkBuilderConditionTests.cs, test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite.Tests/Marks/MarkBuilderTimeTests.cs, test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite.Tests/Marks/MarkBuilderPathTests.cs, test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite.Tests/Marks/MarkBuilderOrderTests.cs, test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite.Tests/Marks/MarkBuilderOverlayTests.cs, test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite.Tests/Marks/MarkBuilderTextTests.cs, test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite.Tests/Marks/MarkBuilderArcTests.cs, test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite.Tests/Marks/MarkBuilderPolarTextTests.cs */
        comment designRef /* Design: docs/design/canvas-net-vega-lite/marks/mark-builder.md */
        comment verificationRef /* Verification: docs/verification/canvas-net-vega-lite/marks/mark-builder.md */
        comment reqRef /* Requirements: docs/reqstream/canvas-net-vega-lite/marks/mark-builder.yaml */
    }
}
